---
import { METRICS } from "../../data/metrics";
import { supplementaryRows } from "../../data/supplementary-results";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const jev = supplementaryRows.find((r) => r.slug === "jev-luna-summaries");
---

<Layout title="Experiments" description="Controlled comparisons that vary the input, harness, or reasoning setting of the benchmark task.">
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-14 sm:px-6">
		<p class="eyebrow">Experiments</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-serif text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Beyond the main benchmark</h1>
		<p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg text-ink-2">
			Controlled comparisons that change one part of the task, such as the input, the harness, or the reasoning setting, on the same {jev?.case_count ?? 91} cases. They are reported separately from the main leaderboard, where every model reads the full record with document tools.
		</p>
		<div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
			<a href="/experiments/summary-pipelines/" class="card group flex flex-col p-6 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-rule-strong hover:shadow-sm">
				<p class="eyebrow">Summary pipelines</p>
				<h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold leading-snug tracking-tight group-hover:text-accent">Jev on case summaries forecast worse than a coin flip</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
					Typesafe.ai's Jev scored a micro Brier of {jev ? METRICS.micro_brier.format(jev.micro_brier) : "n/a"} from GPT-5.6 Luna summaries. OpenAI models given the same summaries beat the base rate, even with reasoning off.
				</p>
				<span class="mt-5 text-sm font-medium text-accent">Read the experiment →</span>
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
